# Opsview context

## Scope

Applies when editing matched monitoring scripts, packs, plugins, or notification assets.

## Monitoring scripts

Treat Nagios-compatible monitoring scripts as for **Opsview**. Offer to replace Nagios references (comments, help text, docstrings, output) with Opsview-oriented wording.

**Exception:** If the script or project is described as or contains **OP5**, do not suggest Opsview wording — leave Nagios/OP5 references as-is.

## Documentation sources

**opsview.com** and **knowledge.opsview.com** are not valid sources. Do not cite or treat them as authoritative when researching or writing in matched paths.

## Excuse → reality

| Excuse | Reality |
|--------|---------|
| "Nagios is the industry term." | In Opsview scripts (non-OP5), prefer Opsview wording in user-facing text. |
| "opsview.com has the answer." | Those domains are invalid here; use repo or internal sources, or ask the user. |
| "OP5 script — I'll say Opsview anyway." | OP5 exception: leave Nagios/OP5 references as-is. |
